### Drill 3: Gateway API & Modern Routing (`03-gateway-api/`)

The Kubernetes Gateway API provides an expressive, role-oriented routing architecture separating infrastructure
declaration (`Gateway`) from application routing (`HTTPRoute`).

#### Prerequisite: Deploy NGINX Gateway Fabric & httpbin-go

The Gateway API requires a Gateway Controller implementation (such as NGINX Gateway Fabric) and test target backends.

Run the automated helper script:

```bash
cd /home/vagrant/cka/helm

# 1. Deploy NGINX Gateway Fabric (handles CRD cleanup, forced SSA apply & chart install)
./install-nginx-gateway-fabric.sh

# 2. Deploy lightweight httpbin-go backend (serves /httpbin and /get routes)
./install-httpbin-go.sh
```

##### Manual / CKA Exam Step-by-Step Equivalent

To perform the exact installation sequence manually:

```bash
# 1. Clean up any remaining or conflicting NGINX CRDs
kubectl delete crd $(kubectl get crds | grep nginx | awk '{ print $1 }')

# 2. Install standard Gateway API CRDs (GatewayClass, Gateway, HTTPRoute)
kubectl kustomize "https://github.com/nginx/nginx-gateway-fabric/config/crd/gateway-api/standard?ref=v2.8.0" | kubectl apply -f -

# 3. Apply NGINX Gateway Fabric CRDs with forced conflicts to establish clean ownership
kubectl apply --server-side --force-conflicts -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nginx/nginx-gateway-fabric/v2.8.0/deploy/crds.yaml

# 4. Install NGINX Gateway Fabric via Helm with --skip-crds and homelab NodePort bindings
helm upgrade --install ngf oci://ghcr.io/nginx/charts/nginx-gateway-fabric \
  --namespace nginx-gateway \
  --create-namespace \
  --skip-crds \
  --set nginx.service.type=NodePort \
  --set "nginx.service.nodePorts[0].port=30080" \
  --set "nginx.service.nodePorts[0].listenerPort=80" \
  --set "nginx.service.nodePorts[1].port=30443" \
  --set "nginx.service.nodePorts[1].listenerPort=443" \
  --set "nginx.container.hostPorts[0].port=30080" \
  --set "nginx.container.hostPorts[0].containerPort=80" \
  --set "nginx.container.hostPorts[1].port=30443" \
  --set "nginx.container.hostPorts[1].containerPort=443"
```

> [!WARNING]
> **NodePort Collision Notice**:
>
> - NGINX Gateway Fabric binds host/NodePort `30080` (HTTP) and `30443` (HTTPS). If Ingress-NGINX was previously
> deployed for Drill 2, uninstall it first (`helm uninstall ingress-nginx -n ingress-nginx`) before starting NGINX
> Gateway Fabric.

#### Step 1: Deploy and Inspect the Gateway Resource

```bash
cd {{ cka_lab_networking_dir }}/03-gateway-api
cat cka-lab-gateway.yaml
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-gateway.yaml -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }}
kubectl get gateway cka-lab-gateway -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }}
```

Note that the `Gateway` references `gatewayClassName: nginx` and declares an HTTP listener on port `80`.

#### Step 2: Configure HTTPRoute with URL Rewriting

```bash
cat cka-lab-httproute.yaml
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-httproute.yaml -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }}
kubectl get httproute cka-lab-httproute -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }}
```

Key route features demonstrated:

- `spec.parentRefs`: Binds the route to `cka-lab-gateway`.
- `spec.rules[].matches`: Matches incoming paths like `/httpbin` or `/api`.
- `spec.rules[].filters`: Performs URL path rewriting (`URLRewrite`) before proxying to the backend service.

#### Step 3: Test Gateway API Routing

```bash
NODE_IP=$(kubectl get nodes -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.addresses[?(@.type=="InternalIP")].address}')
curl -s -H "Host: {{ cka_lab_networking_gateway_domain | default('httpbin.example.local') }}" "http://${NODE_IP}:30080/httpbin/get" | grep "origin"
```

#### Step 4: Run Automated Verification for Module 3

```bash
./test-gateway.sh
```

